# vllm — our own process on a GPU host.
#
# NOT EXERCISED. There is no machine to run this on yet: it needs CUDA, real
# weights, and a provisioned host. `scripts/provision.sh` is a deferred M4 stub
# (docs/BACKLOG.md), which is why this profile has no setup hook — the setup
# *is* provisioning. The backend itself is implemented and covered by the shared
# contract suite in tests/test_backends.py; what is untested is vLLM's own CLI
# accepting these flags and wait_for_vram_release watching real VRAM come back.
#
# The paths below are the packaged defaults from settings.py, i.e. a real host
# rather than this repo. Point HARNESS_MODELS_FILE at a catalog whose entries
# say `backend: vllm` and whose model_ref is the HF repo — see
# docs/BACKENDS.md §4.1 for the full migration, including the per-model `args:`
# (--tool-call-parser, --reasoning-parser) that only this backend passes through.

HARNESS_DEFAULT_BACKEND=vllm
HARNESS_VLLM_BIN=/opt/harness/.venv/bin/vllm
HARNESS_VLLM_PORT=8000
HARNESS_MODELS_FILE=/etc/harness/models.yaml
HARNESS_STATE_DIR=/var/lib/harness
